H1700.definition:
feminine of H1697 (דָּבָר);
a reason, suit or style
KJV: cause, end, estate, order, regard.

H1701.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H1700 (דִּבְרָה)
{a reason, suit or style}
KJV: intent, sake.

H1702.definition:
feminine active participle of H1696 (דָבַר) in the sense of driving (compare H1699 (דֹּבֶר));
a raft
KJV: float.

H1703.definition:
intensive from H1696 (דָבַר);
a word
KJV: word.

H1704.definition:
from H1697 (דָּבָר); wordy;
Dibri, an Israelite
KJV: Dibri.

H1705.definition:
from H1697 (דָּבָר) (perhaps in the sense of H1699 (דֹּבֶר));
Daberath, a place in Palestine
KJV: Dabareh, Daberath.

H1706.definition:
from an unused root meaning to be gummy;
honey (from its stickiness); by analogy, syrup
KJV: honey(-comb).

H1707.definition:
intensive from the same as H1706 (דְּבַשׁ);
a sticky mass, i.e. the hump of acamel
KJV: hunch (of a camel).

H1708.definition:
the same as H1707 (דַּבֶּשֶׁת);
Dabbesheth, a place in Palestine
KJV: Dabbesheth.

H1709.definition:
or (fully) דָּאג; (Nehemiah 13:16), from H1711 (דָּגָה); a fish (as prolific); or perhaps rather from H1672 (דָּאַג) (as timid); but still better from H1672 (דָּאַג) (in the sense of squirming, i.e. moving by the vibratory action of the tail);
a fish (often used collectively)
KJV: fish.

H1710.definition:
feminine of H1709 (דָּג), and meaning the same
{a fish (often used collectively)}
KJV: fish.

H1711.definition:
a primitive root; to move rapidly; used only as a denominative from H1709 (דָּג);
to spawn, i.e. become numerous
KJV: grow.

H1712.definition:
from H1709 (דָּג); the fish-god;
Dagon, a Philistine deity
KJV: Dagon.

H1713.definition:
a primitive root;
to flaunt, i.e. raise a flag; figuratively, to be conspicuous
KJV: (set up, with) banners, chiefest.

H1714.definition:
from H1713 (דָּגַל);
a flag
KJV: banner, standard.

H1715.definition:
from H1711 (דָּגָה);
properly, increase, i.e. grain
KJV: corn (floor), wheat.

H1717.definition:
apparently from the same as H1730 (דּוֹד);
the breast (as the seat of love, or from its shape)
KJV: breast, teat.

H1718.definition:
a doubtful root;
to walk gently
KJV: go (softly, with).

H1719.definition:
or (prolonged) דְּדָנֶה; (Ezekiel 25:13), of uncertain derivation;
Dedan, the name of two Cushites and of their territory
KJV: Dedan.

H1720.definition:
plural of H1719 (דְּדָן) (as patrial);
Dedanites, the descendants or inhabitants of Dedan
KJV: Dedanim.

H1721.definition:
or (by orthographical error) רֹדָנִים (1 Chronicles 1:7); a plural of uncertain derivation;
Dodanites, or descendants of a son of Javan
KJV: Dodanim.

H1722.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H2091 (זָהָב);
gold
KJV: gold(-en).

H1723.definition:
(Aramaic) of uncertain derivation;
Dahava, a people colonized in Samaria
KJV: Dehavites.

H1724.definition:
a primitive root (compare H1740 (דּוּחַ));
to be dumb, i.e. (figuratively) dumbfounded
KJV: astonished.

H1725.definition:
a primitive root;
to curvet or move irregularly
KJV: pause.

H1726.definition:
by reduplication from H1725 (דָּהַר);
a gallop
KJV: pransing.

H1727.definition:
a primitive root;
to mope, i.e. (figuratively) pine
KJV: sorrow.

H1728.definition:
an orthographical variation of H1709 (דָּג) as a denominative (H1771 (דַּיָּג));
a fisherman
KJV: fisher.

H1729.definition:
feminine from the same as H1728 (דַּוָּג);
properly, fishery, i.e. a hook forfishing
KJV: fish (hook).

H1731.definition:
from the same as H1730 (דּוֹד);
a pot (for boiling); also (by resemblance of shape) a basket
KJV: basket, caldron, kettle, (seething) pot.

H1732.definition:
rarely (fully); דָּוִיד; from the same as H1730 (דּוֹד); loving;
David, the youngest son of Jesse
KJV: David.

H1733.definition:
feminine of H1730 (דּוֹד);
an aunt
KJV: aunt, father's sister, uncle's wife.

H1734.definition:
from H1730 (דּוֹד); loving;
Dodo, the name of three Israelites
KJV: Dodo.

H1735.definition:
from H1730 (דּוֹד) and H3050 (יָהּ); love of Jah;
Dodavah, an Israelite
KJV: Dodavah.

H1736.definition:
from H1731 (דּוּד);
a boiler or basket; also the mandrake (as an aphrodisiac)
KJV: basket, mandrake.

H1737.definition:
formed like H1736 (דּוּדַי); amatory;
Dodai, an Israelite
KJV: Dodai.

H1738.definition:
a primitive root;
to be sick (as if in menstruation)
KJV: infirmity.

H1739.definition:
from H1738 (דָּוָה);
sick (especially in menstruation)
KJV: faint, menstruous cloth, she that is sick, having sickness.

H1740.definition:
a primitive root;
to thrust away; figuratively, to cleanse
KJV: cast out, purge, wash.

H1741.definition:
from H1739 (דָּוֶה);
sickness; figuratively, loathing
KJV: languishing, sorrowful.

H1742.definition:
from H1739 (דָּוֶה);
sick; figuratively, troubled
KJV: faint.

H1743.definition:
a primitive root;
to bruise in a mortar
KJV: beat.

H1744.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
the hoopoe or else the grouse
KJV: lapwing.

H1745.definition:
from an unused root meaning to be dumb (compare H1820 (דָּמָה));
silence; figuratively, death
KJV: silence.

H1746.definition:
the same as H1745 (דּוּמָה);
Dumah, a tribe and region of Arabia
KJV: Dumah.

H1747.definition:
from H1820 (דָּמָה);
stillness; adverbially, silently; abstractly quiet, trust
KJV: silence, silent, waiteth.

H1748.definition:
from H1826 (דָּמַם);
still; adverbially, silently
KJV: dumb, silent, quietly wait.

H1749.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
wax;
KJV: wax.

H1750.definition:
a primitive root;
to leap
KJV: be turned.

H1751.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H1854 (דָּקַק);
to crumble
KJV: be broken to pieces.

H1752.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to gyrate (or move in a circle), i.e. to remain
KJV: dwell.

H1753.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H1752 (דּוּר);
to reside
KJV: dwell.

H1754.definition:
from H1752 (דּוּר);
a circle, ball or pile
KJV: ball, turn, round about.

H1755.definition:
or (shortened) דֹּר; from H1752 (דּוּר);
properly, a revolution of time, i.e. an age or generation; also a dwelling
KJV: age, [idiom] evermore, generation, (n-) ever, posterity.

H1756.definition:
or (by permutation) דֹּאר; (Joshua 17:11; 1 Kings 4:11), from H1755 (דּוֹר); dwelling;
Dor, a place in Palestine
KJV: Dor.

H1757.definition:
(Aramaic) probably from H1753 (דּוּר); circle or dwelling;
Dura, a place in Babylonia
KJV: Dura.

H1758.definition:
or דּוֹשׁ; or דִּישׁ; a primitive root;
to trample or thresh
KJV: break, tear, thresh, tread out (down), at grass (Jeremiah 50:11, by mistake for H1877 (דֶּשֶׁא)).

H1759.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H1758 (דּוּשׁ);
to trample
KJV: tread down.

H1760.definition:
or דָּחַח; (Jeremiah 23:12), a primitive root;
to push down
KJV: chase, drive away (on), overthrow, outcast, [idiom] sore, thrust, totter.

H1761.definition:
(Aramaic) from the equivalent of H1760 (דָּחָה);
probably a musical instrument (as being struck)
KJV: instrument of music.

H1762.definition:
from H1760 (דָּחָה);
a push, i.e. (by implication) a fall
KJV: falling.

H1763.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H2119 (זָחַל);
to slink, i.e. (by implication) to fear, or (causatively) be formidable
KJV: make afraid, dreadful, fear, terrible.

H1764.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
millet
KJV: millet.

H1765.definition:
a primitive root;
to urge, i.e. hasten
KJV: (be) haste(-ned), pressed on.

H1766.definition:
a primitive root;
to press, i.e. oppress
KJV: thrust, vex.

H1767.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
enough (as noun or adverb), used chiefly with preposition in phrases
KJV: able, according to, after (ability), among, as (oft as), (more than) enough, from, in, since, (much as is) sufficient(-ly), too much, very, when.

H1768.definition:
(Aramaic) apparently for H1668 (דָּא);
that, used as relative conjunction, and especially (with a preposition) in adverbial phrases; also as preposition of
KJV: [idiom] as, but, for(-asmuch [phrase]), [phrase] now, of, seeing, than, that, therefore, until, [phrase] what (-soever), when, which, whom, whose.

H1770.definition:
denominative from H1709 (דָּג);
to fish
KJV: fish.

H1771.definition:
from H1770 (דִּיג);
a fisherman
KJV: fisher.

H1772.definition:
intensive from H1675 (דָּאָה);
a falcon (from its rapid flight)
KJV: vulture.

H1773.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
ink
KJV: ink.

H1774.definition:
as if from H1768 (דִּי) and H2091 (זָהָב); of gold;
Dizahab, a place in the Desert
KJV: Dizahab.

H1775.definition:
perhaps for H1769 (דִּיבוֹן);
Dimon, a place in Palestine
KJV: Dimon.

H1776.definition:
feminine of H1775 (דִּימוֹן);
Dimonah, a place in Palestine
KJV: Dimonah.

H1777.definition:
or (Genesis 6:3) דּוּן; a primitive root;
a straight course, i.e. sail direct
KJV: (come) with a straight course.

H1778.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H1777 (דִּין);
to judge
KJV: judge.

H1779.definition:
or (Job 19:29) דּוּן; from H1777 (דִּין);
judgement (the suit, justice, sentence or tribunal); by implication also strife
KJV: cause, judgement, plea, strife.

H1780.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H1779 (דִּין)
{judgement (the suit, justice, sentence or tribunal); by implication also strife}
KJV: judgement.

H1781.definition:
from H1777 (דִּין);
a judge or advocate
KJV: judge.

H1782.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H1781 (דַּיָּן)
{a judge or advocate}
KJV: judge.

H1783.definition:
feminine of H1779 (דִּין); justice;
Dinah, the daughter of Jacob
KJV: Dinah.

H1784.definition:
(Aramaic) partial from uncertain primitive;
a Dinaite or inhabitant of some unknown Assyria province
KJV: Dinaite.

H1785.definition:
from a root corresp. to H1751 (דּוּק);
a battering-tower
KJV: fort.

H1787.definition:
(Diyshon, the same as H1788 (דִּישֹׁן);
Dishon, the name of two Edomites
KJV: Dishon.

H1788.definition:
from H1758 (דּוּשׁ);
the leaper, i.e. an antelope
KJV: pygarg.

H1790.definition:
from an unused root (compare H1794 (דָּכָה));
crushed, i.e. (figuratively) injured
KJV: afflicted, oppressed.

H1791.definition:
(Aramaic) or דָּךְ; (Aramaic), prolonged from H1668 (דָּא);
this
KJV: the same, this.

H1792.definition:
a primitive root (compare H1794 (דָּכָה));
to crumble; transitively, to bruise (literally or figuratively)
KJV: beat to pieces, break (in pieces), bruise, contrite, crush, destroy, humble, oppress, smite.

H1793.definition:
from H1792 (דָּכָא);
crushed (literally powder, or figuratively, contrite)
KJV: contrite, destruction.

H1794.definition:
a primitive root (compare H1790 (דַּךְ), H1792 (דָּכָא));
to collapse (phys. or mentally)
KJV: break (sore), contrite, crouch.

H1795.definition:
from H1794 (דָּכָה) like H1793 (דַּכָּא);
mutilated
KJV: [phrase] wounded.

H1796.definition:
from H1794 (דָּכָה);
a dashing of surf
KJV: wave.

H1797.definition:
(Aramaic) prolonged from H1791 (דֵּךְ);
this
KJV: same, that, this.

H1798.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H2145 (זָכָר);
properly, a male, i.e. of sheep
KJV: ram.

H1799.definition:
(Aramaic) or דׇּכְרָן (Aramaic); corresponding to H2146 (זִכְרוֹן);
a register
KJV: record.
